From: rnsbox <rnsbox@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: sophgo: sg2000-milkv-duo-s: enable uart1 for SLIP

The board did not expose /dev/ttyS1 at all: the SoC dtsi leaves uart1
disabled and no board patch enabled it. Turn it on so S31slip can attach
the line discipline to the HaLow modem.

The disppll/cam0_200 reclock is deliberately NOT part of this patch: the
clk driver's disppll set_rate hangs in of_clk_init() before the
console registers on CV18xx. The vendor bootloader leaves cam0_200 at
25 MHz, so the UART stays at its 1,562,500 ceiling and slip.conf ships
1.5 Mbaud until the vendor 768 MHz LUT path is ported upstream.
The XGPIOA[28]/[29] fmux is still set by S31slip at boot.

---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2000-milkv-duo-s.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2000-milkv-duo-s.dts
index 9fa77ba..b5d43ab 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2000-milkv-duo-s.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2000-milkv-duo-s.dts
@@ -242,3 +242,7 @@
 	dr_mode = "peripheral";
 	status = "okay";
 };
+
+&uart1 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
-- 
2.43.0
